"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act4_ch23.md — do not edit */

SC["a4c23_descent"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TWENTY-THREE — THE GRAND LOOM`)+P(`The invitation to the floor itself comes from the Lady's own page: white silk, no words at all, just a woven map: the spiral stair, continued past the warp-galleries, down below the lakebed. Suyin reads it over your shoulder and goes quiet in a new way.`)+P(`“Forty years,” she says, “and I've been to the floor four times. The Lady doesn't show the Loom to people she's bargaining with. She shows it to people she's already counted.” Her hands sort the silk map's threads as if tidying a child's hair. “Go down, stitch. Count yourself differently. It's the only argument that's ever worked on her.”`)+((G.f.a4_route=="prisoner")?(P(`The guards who fetch you have given up pretending you're cargo: they walk behind you on the stair, at honor-guard distance, and the younger one carries your silk tag on a tray, as if it were a hat you might want back.`)):(""))+P(`The stair leaves the piling and becomes a ramp of fused white silk, wide as a road, and the water-pressure builds against the crystal walls until the dark outside is total. Then the ramp opens out, and the dark inside ends.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The floor of the world.`,go:"a4c23_loom"}]};

SC["a4c23_loom"]={img:"loom",
 t:()=>P(`No one warned you, because there are no words that would have worked.`)+P(`The Grand Loom fills a drowned valley. You stand on a gallery at its rim and the far side is WEATHER, not architecture: warp-lines in their hundreds of thousands rising out of bedrock anchors, running up into the lake-dark like rain reversed, every one of them alight with the pale dawn-color of working soul-silk, so that the whole valley glows the way paper lanterns glow, from within, acres of it, a sea floor made of light. Shuttle-bridges the size of villages move along the weft on schedules forty years long. Reels turn overhead, slow as moons. The chord you felt in the gallery is a body-blow down here, one note, four hundred years sustained, and your threads answer it whether you ask them to or not: gold rising off your sleeves toward all that pale fire like iron filings finding north.`)+P(`It is the largest made thing you have seen in two worlds, and the second-truest. Some part of you that has been keeping score since a bus stop in the rain quietly puts the score away.`)+P(`And beneath it — pinned under the warp like a wound under sutures, visible in glimpses between the light — the GREAT FRAY. The founding calamity. A tear in the Weave of Heaven the size of a province, four centuries old, its edges white and dead where the Loom's tension has bled them numb. It does not wave like Yu-le's little tear waved. It strains, continuously, against a quarter-million lines, with the patience of a thing that has nowhere else to be.`)+P(`You stand there long enough that your legs inform you about it afterward. Counting. Reading. Doing the one sum that matters.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Stay through the watch-change and run the full tension-sum, line-class by line-class, until your eyes stream.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);note("+1 Insight. The warp's true load runs through the woven elders \u2014 a few hundred fans of willing thread \u2014 and through the bedrock, and through nothing else. The furnace-heat keeps the DEAD lines supple: forty generations of accumulated pattern that a living warp would simply replace. Suyin's arithmetic, confirmed at scale: rebuild the center, and the sky stays up on willing shoulders. The fuel was never the load.");},go:"a4c23_sum"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Let the scale be scale. Some things you stand in front of; the counting can wait for the books.`,do:()=>{G.heart++;note("+1 Heart. You give the largest made thing in two worlds one hour of plain witness, no arithmetic at all \u2014 and you understand the believers a little better forever after, which will matter more than any sum you'd have run.");},go:"a4c23_sum"}]};

SC["a4c23_sum"]={t:()=>P(`The Loom's index finds you before you go looking for it, because the index is not a room. It is a REEL: the first reel ever wound, black with age, turning alone in a shrine-niche at the gallery's end, and on it, in thread, the name and nature of every stitch the Loom has ever counted — consignments, elders, officers, debts. The ledger of ledgers. Four hundred years of Kang's little book, perfected.`)+P(`The white thread on a beloved shoulder answers it from half a city above: you feel the claim go taut, politely, like a clerk looking up at a customer.`)+((G.f.a3_marked=="sho")?(P(`Here, then. Granny Sho's name is ON this reel, written the night Madam Xian's sleeve moved on a riverhouse dock. It can be unwritten the same way: you can see the claim's anchor-knot from where you stand, one white loop among millions, and your gold could have it out in an hour's careful work. Or it can stay, because a claim the Court believes in is also a leash the Court believes in, and leashes run both ways, and no one watches a fish they've already netted.`)):(P(`Here, then. Ruan's name is ON this reel, written the night Madam Xian's sleeve moved on a riverhouse dock. It can be unwritten: the claim's anchor-knot hangs one white loop among millions, an hour's careful gold. Or it can stay, because a claim the Court believes in is also a leash the Court believes in, and leashes run both ways, and no one watches a fish they've already netted.`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Unpick the claim NOW. The Court can know. Some things don't stay owed.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_unmarked=true;note("An hour's work, the finest you've ever done, and the white loop opens and is nothing. Half a city above, a thread slides off a shoulder and drops. The black reel ticks once, like a clock noticing. The Court will know by morning. Let them. Some pages don't stay written.");},go:"a4c23_lady"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Leave it written — a known leash is cover, and you can cut it the hour it matters.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_unmarked=false;note("You memorize the anchor-knot instead: its turns, its tension, the hour of work it will take on the day it matters. The claim stays on the page, and the Court stays sure of its surety. Ruan would call this keeping a liability on the books at a known address. He'd approve. It still tastes like swallowing a coin.");},go:"a4c23_lady"}]};

SC["a4c23_lady"]={t:()=>P(`The reels speak.`)+P(`Not one voice from one place: the same voice from EVERY reel in earshot — the shrine-niche, the gallery rims, the moon-slow towers overhead — a woman's voice, even and unhurried and very old, arriving from all directions at once the way light arrives in the valley.`)+P(`“The mountain's gold thread. Stand where I can feel you, little stitch.”`)+P(`You stand where you are, since everywhere is that.`)+P(`“I am the First Reel. I had a name; the warp has it now.” The valley's light shifts, minutely, a cathedral adjusting its attention. “Four hundred years ago the sky of this land TORE, and I was the only weaver who answered it, and I answered it with everything I had and everything I could take. I have heard every argument you are carrying since before your grandmother's grandmother. The young Reels bring them to me each generation, on fire, certain. The fray is real — you have seen it. The Loom holds — you are standing on the proof. And the price is monstrous. All three are true. I have had four centuries to find a fourth truth that unmakes the third.” A reel near your shoulder turns once, dry as Granny Sho. “There isn't one. There is only the sum: a thousand souls a generation, against the sky of the heartland. I do that sum every day. I have never once liked it.”`)+P(`“And now the warp tells me a boy walks my floor with a pattern-sense the Loom has wanted for four hundred years. So here is the invitation, from the only mouth that means it whole: the Loom remembers its stitches, weaver. Come be remembered PROPERLY. Take the heart-position when I finally fray. Hold the sky the way I held it — better, with those hands. The work is real. The need is real. You have seen both.”`)+P(`“Or bring me your fourth truth, if the mountain taught you one. I have been waiting four hundred years to be wrong, and nobody competent has ever once managed it.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`“Then keep waiting, Lady. I'm going to need a bigger loom.”`,go:"a4c23_after"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Say nothing. Bow to the black reel, the way you'd bow to a worthy enemy's grave.`,do:()=>{G.heart++;note("+1 Heart. You bow, and the valley's light holds still through it, and for one moment the voice from every reel says nothing at all \u2014 which, from a woman four hundred years certain, is the loudest thing in the room.");},go:"a4c23_after"}]};

SC["a4c23_after"]={t:()=>P(`The climb back up takes an hour, and you spend it rearranging everything you thought the act would be.`)+P(`You came upriver carrying an enemy shaped like a court. What the valley showed you is worse and better: an enemy shaped like a SUM — one woman's four-hundred-year arithmetic, honestly run, monstrously priced, defended by believers because it has never once been beaten. Madam Xian tithes herself to it. Suyin holds a province of it. The Lady IS it, mostly thread, doing the hateful math daily and waiting, in some fossil chamber of herself, for a competent wrongness.`)+P(`The counter-pattern isn't a heist anymore. It's a PROOF. You will have to beat the sum in front of the whole Court, with a better one.`)+((G.f.a4_unmarked)?(SYS(`The claim is unwritten; the surety walks free. The Court will file it as a declaration of intent, because it is one. The black reel keeps your hour of gold on its page instead.`)):(SYS(`The claim stays written, and you hold its anchor-knot memorized: one hour of gold, payable the day it matters. The Court suspects nothing. Ruan-style bookkeeping, on the Court's own reel.`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Morning brings sails on the lake: grey ones, mountain-cut. The Azure Cloud has arrived.`,go:"a4c24_arrival"}]};